# dsv41 + core: a broken rank pair ends the server instead of hanging it. Without this patch, rank 0 of the stock engine
# waits forever when rank 1 dies or hangs: requests stay stuck, the ranks fall out of sync, and no supervisor can
# restart a process that never exits. comm.zig abortAll: ncclCommAbort (looked up in the libnccl already loaded) and the
# RDMA rings' abort word, safe from any thread and never under an enqueue (a gate), after which every collective refuses
# (CommAborted); RingFailed is fatal. TF_DS_PAIR_BROKEN=exit, the default (unset or empty), admits nothing new, fails
# everything that waits at once ("the engine's rank pair broke (<cause>); the server restarts"), lets streams that can
# still run finish for 5 s, aborts the communicator and exits with status 75 for the service's supervisor to restart
# both ranks (the recipe's systemd user service, docs/systemd.md, restarts on any failure; without a supervisor the
# server stays down instead of hanging); rank 0's start-up log says so. degrade opts out: the behaviour before this
# patch (requests fail one by one, the spill tier stops, the server stays up); anything else is refused at start. A
# follower whose process ended (killed, crashed) closes its link at once: rank 0 watches the followers' links
# (link.Watch: POLLRDHUP, a hang-up or a reset, looked at every 100 ms) and, 500 ms later (a stop of both ranks at once
# ends as a shutdown), stops the collectives, so a round blocked on the dead peer returns, and breaks the pair with
# nothing to drain. A follower that hangs keeps its socket open: a stall monitor breaks the pair when the engine thread
# is busy without progress for 120 s. The exit is enforced 15 s after a break (both bounds fixed), and a clean shutdown
# that meets a break still finishes. /health answers 503 "stalled" or "broken" past those bounds; /health and /metrics
# count service_refused and pair_failed. A restore the tier refuses only for capacity (Tier.full, TierFull: the restores
# in flight hold the room) waits up to TF_SPILL_DEFER_MS (5000; 0: never) instead of prefilling from 0, counted in
# restores_deferred.
# Switches: TF_DS_PAIR_BROKEN unset (exit; degrade opts out), TF_SPILL_DEFER_MS 5000. A server without followers has no
# pair and no policy. The policy acts only after a failure, so replies are unchanged: exact.py 39/39 identical with it
# armed (spill and KV sharding on, which armed it before it became the default: the series with the display-reserve
# patch beside it) and with it off (every switch off, engine 8d26890, before the rebase onto 0008); every switch at its
# default, which now arms it, is still to be run on the pair. Host test: a follower killed mid-round (its socket closed
# while rank 0's round waits on it) ends the pair, its streams failed and one exit 75, within a second. On the pair
# (spill and KV sharding on), rank 1 killed with kill -9 under 8 decoding streams: every stream ended 1.29 s later (the
# link watch; the stall monitor alone had caught it at +135 s), /health went down at 1.78 s and rank 0 exited 75; a stop
# of both ranks ended as a shutdown (exit 0). Builds on 0014, 0018 and 0019. By Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
# Apache-2.0.
